  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Women's song genre of Bissau and Bolama, sung in Guinea-Bissau Kriol at community gatherings and celebrations and named after its central instrument, the tina, a calabash floated upside down in a tub of water and struck. Hand claps and call-and-response singing complete the texture; singer Karyna Gomes has recorded tina repertoire and a 2023 AMI manual documents the genre. The inverted-calabash card stands in for the water drum.",
